{"title":"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c938e3f9dea789595c6290070f7975f45bc4300a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> are periodic with least period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. What is the least period of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/6461b51571bec4ca17a6ab0ca0105cf872c2dfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\sin(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df0543a40af59ee9f611d3b47cda294e53f379a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"363\" height=\"33\" /> The function is not periodic.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2fa440df4c6dc36c257fb9ae25e0b3063d34ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(-x)=\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />. Then realize that under this function, the negative sine values yield the same as their positive value, so take the absolute value of the sine function to get the new period. This has period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can eliminate D and E, as both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> are periodic with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, as stated. Therefore the nested function must be periodic with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e50c5722749a03ed7bd06d6edd5c906363e287b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\le 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />. Next, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> have ranges of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c3818b9565a33fd3aadba10026d32c5e3eea90f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> with turning points/zeroes at values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6def053fc1efb798cc941f5079f8b94da8ff4fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\pi, \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />. These 4 values are easy to compute and should convey the relevant information about our function, so let's consider these.\n</p><p>First compute the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe528b31184b7c72fdb95893a504c06e606dcf97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1, 0, -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> over the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/6461b51571bec4ca17a6ab0ca0105cf872c2dfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\sin(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3e9e0eb25c0b0972c5be2d5185da2f20e0a544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, \\cos(1), 1, \\cos(-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />. You may notice that one appears twice: at the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/94816ab8a73eb77d27708b62b38cea1840d30ae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pi$\" width=\"45\" height=\"8\" />, and guess that the period is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Alternatively, you can use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2fa440df4c6dc36c257fb9ae25e0b3063d34ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(-x)=\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> as in solution 1, which can be shown by considering the unit circle definition of cosine. You then get that the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/6461b51571bec4ca17a6ab0ca0105cf872c2dfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\sin(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/16134920b285afe501f68e6cda29aacfd1133bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, \\cos(1), 1, \\cos(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />, which is more obviously periodic with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>NOTE: This method is not strict proof that the function has period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> as we only consider 4 values in the interval.\n</p><p>~rawr3507\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B\">2017 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190811\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 252/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5451/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.421      1 -total\n 60.61%    8.134      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.66%    5.054      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15450:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190811 and revision id 230616. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}